=== ISSUE ===
Title: update_arena / update_swiss allow partial updates, but Lichess requires clock and duration fields on every edit

Per the Lichess API spec (https://github.com/lichess-org/api/blob/906d1a6e93ca1ba4b65c9decb3077f2431c6d55a/doc/specs/lichess-api.yaml):
- `POST /api/tournament/{id}` requires `clockTime`, `clockIncrement` and `minutes`.
- `POST /api/swiss/{id}/edit` requires `clock.limit`, `clock.increment` and `nbRounds`.

`update_arena` makes all three optional. `update_swiss` makes `nbRounds` optional and can't send the clock at all. So a partial update, such as just renaming, sends a request the spec says is invalid.

=== PR ===
Title: fix: require the fields Lichess needs on arena and Swiss edits
Body:
Closes #<issue>

- `update_arena`: `clockTime`, `clockIncrement` and `minutes` are required.
- `update_swiss`: `clock { limit, increment }` and `nbRounds` are required; clock is sent as `clock.limit` / `clock.increment`, matching `create_swiss`.
- The descriptions point the model to `get_arena_info` / `get_swiss_info` for the current values.

Spec: https://github.com/lichess-org/api/blob/906d1a6e93ca1ba4b65c9decb3077f2431c6d55a/doc/specs/lichess-api.yaml

